            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative evaluation of the effectiveness of various narcotic analgesics after intravenous autoanalgesia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The article is devoted to an investigation of intravenous analgesia with different narcotic analgetic drugs (phentanyl, morphine, dipidolor). A comparative assessment of the influence upon central hemodynamics, lung ventilation, acid-base metabolism and blood gases was performed, as well as the degree of analgesia in using these drugs. A conclusion is made that morphine and phentanyl are preferable for the intravenous postoperative autoanalgesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
